    "Lantern jellies drifted over the gulf. Brask had called them lights, and that was what they were, great soft bells of pale blue fire the size of houses, trailing veils that glimmered and went out and glimmered again."
    "Nothing moved fast. Nothing made a sound. He had come from a forest that never stopped singing to a place that seemed to be holding its breath."

    "Okonta's passengers were met at the landing. Two healers in grey had come up from the Well for the old man from Fallow, as though they had known he was coming. They had a litter with them, slung between two lantern jellies on cords."
    "The daughter went with it. She looked back at Wrack once from the edge. Then they sank away into the black, the two blue lights growing small, toward the star."

