    with dissolve
    "The house stood a little way along the shelf, where the rock broke the surface."

    "It was half in the water and half out of it, under a sky the colour of a pigeon's breast, with a low red sun rolling along the rim of the world. There was a line of washing, quite stiff with frost."
    "At one end was a workshop with its door standing open on a clutter of half-mended things. A kettle sat on the step. There were no guards and no gates."

    "It was empty."

