    "So he sat with his hand in the water and asked, as politely as he knew how, and for three days nothing happened. On the fourth he felt the shelf. He felt it not under his hand but all of it, the whole curve, as though his hand had grown. He felt the weed on it, and a crab walking."
    "The next day he felt the jellies, each a slow cold pulse. The day after that he reached down into the Well as far as he dared. Something very large was coiled against the wall a kilometre below him, and it had felt him too. He took his hand out of the water quickly."

    "His eyes went often to the workshop door. His hands wanted to go in. He did not let them."

