    "One hall of the nine was dark. It was cracked from roof to floor, and the sea stood in it. The centre of the ring had been stove in. The dart was still there. It was sunk to half its length in the floor above the heart, a pale sliver no longer than a man, and it was humming faintly."
    "The healers had not left their pools. They sat at every one with their hands in the water, three to a pool, in what light there was. Some of them were weeping. None of them had moved."

